{"name":"Mineral Deposit","hex":"#abb0ac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mineral","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any naturally occurring solid material that has a (more or less) definite chemical composition and characteristic physical properties; especially, an inorganic and crystalline one.","Any inorganic material (as distinguished from animal or vegetable)."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["of, related to, or containing minerals"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mineral"},{"term":"deposit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Sediment or rock that is not native to its present location or is different from the surrounding material. Sometimes refers to ore or gems.","Bailment of personal property to be kept gratuitously for the bailor (depositor) and without any benefit to the bailee (depositary), e.g. for storage, carriage, repair, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lay down; to place; to put.","To lay up or away for safekeeping; to put up; to store."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deposit"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ore","blocks":[{"text":"Ore is natural rock or sediment that contains one or more valuable minerals, typically including metals, concentrated above background levels, and that is economically viable to mine and process. Ore grade refers to the concentration of the desired material it contains. The value of the metals or minerals a rock contains must be weighed against the cost of extraction to determine whether it is of sufficiently high grade to be worth mining and is therefore considered an ore. A complex ore is one containing more than one valuable mineral."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Banded_iron_formation.png/330px-Banded_iron_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ore","wikidata":"Q102798"},{"title":"Mineral","blocks":[{"text":"In geology and mineralogy, a mineral or mineral species is, broadly speaking, a solid substance with a fairly well-defined chemical composition and a specific crystal structure that occurs naturally in pure form."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/S%C3%A9randite%2C_natrolite%2C_analcime%2C_aegirine_300-4-2112.JPG/330px-S%C3%A9randite%2C_natrolite%2C_analcime%2C_aegirine_300-4-2112.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mineral","wikidata":"Q7946"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Psilomelane-167850.jpg/500px-Psilomelane-167850.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Psilomelane-167850.jpg/500px-Psilomelane-167850.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Manganese ore – psilomelane (size: 6.7 × 5.8 × 5.1 cm)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APsilomelane-167850.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Anglesite-Galena-249200.jpg/500px-Anglesite-Galena-249200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Anglesite-Galena-249200.jpg/500px-Anglesite-Galena-249200.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lead ore – galena and anglesite (size: 4.8 × 4.0 × 3.0 cm)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnglesite-Galena-249200.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Grainitic_Pegmatite.jpg/500px-Grainitic_Pegmatite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Grainitic_Pegmatite.jpg/1280px-Grainitic_Pegmatite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x